/-
  THE FACTOR — factoriality of the tower limit and the full modular spectrum:
  the operator-level type-III₁ signature (LIMIT ALGEBRA campaign, brick LA2).

  With the full commutation equality J·M·J = M′ in hand (D2a,
  `tomita_commutation_equality`), this brick delivers the two operator-level statements
  that upgrade the T3 ARITHMETIC Araki–Woods fingerprint to statements about the actual
  von Neumann algebra of the tower:

  PART 1 — FACTORIALITY (`center_eq_scalar`, `towerLimitVN_factor`): Z(M) = ℂ·1.
  1. MIRRORED RIGHT-BIMODULARITY: the stage subspace `V_C` absorbs right multiplication
     (`towerRightMul_stageGermL`: R_a(germ x) = germ(x·a)), and the right stage action at a
     fixed stage is ⋆-closed (T0_4's computed adjoint `(R_a)† = R_{(rightConj² a)ᴴ}` is again
     a stage-C right multiplication) — so the stage projection `P_C` commutes with every
     right stage multiplication (`starProjection_comm_towerRightMul`, the C1
     invariant-projection engine mirrored).
  2. THE CENTRAL-SYMBOL CHASE (`central_symbol_commutes`): for `T ∈ M ∩ M′` with compressed
     symbol `b_C := commutantSymbol T C`,
       LEFT  (D2a's chase):  germ(a·b_C) = π_C(a)(P_C(TΩ)) = P_C(T(germ a));
       RIGHT (the mirror):   germ(b_C·a) = R_a(P_C(TΩ)) = P_C(R_a(TΩ)) = P_C(T(R_aΩ))
                             = P_C(T(germ a))   [T ∈ M commutes with R_a — S6],
     so `germ(a·b_C) = germ(b_C·a)` and germ injectivity forces `b_C` CENTRAL in the stage
     matrix algebra.
  3. STAGE CENTERS ARE TRIVIAL (`stage_central_eq_smul_one`): the center of the full matrix
     algebra is ℂ·1 (the two-line matrix-unit argument, entrywise).
  4. THE SCALAR IS CONSTANT IN THE STAGE: `P_C(TΩ) = λ_C•Ω` with
     `λ_C = ⟪Ω, P_C(TΩ)⟫ = ⟪P_CΩ, TΩ⟫ = ⟪Ω, TΩ⟫` — CONSTANT (P_C self-adjoint, P_CΩ = Ω),
     so `P_C(TΩ) = λ•Ω` for EVERY stage; the stage projections converge strongly to 1, so
     `TΩ = λ•Ω` exactly (no limit of scalars is ever taken).
  5. ★ Ω SEPARATES: `(T − λ•1)Ω = 0` with `T − λ•1 ∈ M` gives `T = λ•1` — THE TOWER LIMIT
     IS A FACTOR (trivial center, `HasTrivialCenter` — the honest formulation; Mathlib has
     no `IsFactor` API).

  PART 2 — THE FULL MODULAR SPECTRUM (under the T3 two-frequency irrational-ratio
  hypotheses, stated through the BOUNDED resolvent R = (1+Δ)⁻¹):
  6. THE EIGENVALUE SUPPLY: the pure matrix-unit components are eigenvectors of Δ with
     eigenvalues the Gibbs ratios w_n/w_m (ID2) and of R with eigenvalues (1+w_n/w_m)⁻¹;
     the ratio formula `gibbsWeight_div_eq_exp_sum` computes every achievable log-ratio,
     and — given two frequencies s, t on infinitely many modes with `Irrational (s/t)`,
     link dimensions ≥ 2, and β ≠ 0 — realizes EVERY point of the subgroup generated by
     βs and βt (`exists_gibbs_ratio_realizing`), which is DENSE by Kronecker (T2's
     `dense_closure_pair`). Eigenvalues of the bounded self-adjoint R lie in its spectrum;
     `σ_ℝ(R) ⊆ [0,1]` is held (R2); the spectrum is closed and contains a dense subset of
     (0,1), hence
       ★ `spectrum_towerResolvent_eq_Icc` : σ_ℝ(R) = [0,1] EXACTLY,
     and at the Δ level the closure of the point spectrum is exactly [0,∞)
     (★ `modular_spectrum_full`) — the FULL modular spectrum for the tower state, read
     through the resolvent correspondence δ ↔ (1+δ)⁻¹, with no unbounded-spectrum API used.
  7. ★★ THE CAPSTONE (`operator_level_III1_signature`, hypothesis-free √2 instance
     `operator_level_III1_signature_sqrtTwo`): the conjunction — the tower limit is a
     FACTOR ∧ the modular operator is NOT the identity (Δ ≠ 1, the N3 non-triviality) ∧
     the modular spectrum is FULL (σ(R) = [0,1], i.e. spec Δ = [0,∞) in the resolvent
     sense). THE OPERATOR-LEVEL III₁ SIGNATURE: the strongest honest statement without a
     type API — for a type-III₁ factor this is exactly the expected signature (factor,
     non-tracial, S(M) = [0,∞)), but here it is established for THE TOWER STATE's modular
     operator only.

  MANDATORY FIREWALL (binding): the Connes S-INVARIANT PROPER (the infimum of modular
  spectra over ALL faithful normal states) and the TYPE CLASSIFICATION are ABSENT — no
  type API exists in any proof assistant; Araki–Woods 1968 and Connes 1973 are CITED,
  never invoked. The spectrum statement is for the TOWER STATE's modular operator — one
  distinguished state, not an infimum over states — which is exactly why this is a
  SIGNATURE and not a classification. Finite-stage Gibbs inductive limit only (ITPFI-type
